{"step_index":329,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-01T17:02:07Z","thinking":"Examining the docstring, the escape sequence necessitates a correction; using a raw string or forward slashes resolves the potential issue. Focusing on the `chart_canvas.py` file, the bottom axis needs modification to display time labels rather than numerical values, requiring the creation of a `TimeAxisItem` and its connection to the bottom plot. Subsequent steps will involve integrating this time axis into the `ChartCanvas` class itself.\n\n\nNow focusing on the candlestick plotting, data will be prepared as tuples containing index and OHLC data, and time labels will be extracted from the candlestick data. The `TimeAxisItem` needs a method to set labels and another to convert axis values to strings based on these labels. The `tickStrings` method will be critical for handling axis tick display, taking into account potential floating-point tick values provided by the library. The code should consider the case where the values are very close.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":".venv\\Scripts\\python.exe -c \"import pyqtgraph as pg; from PyQt6.QtWidgets import QApplication; app = QApplication([]); axis = pg.AxisItem('bottom'); print('Axis created successfully')\"","Cwd":"Y:\\SIGNAL","WaitMsBeforeAsync":5000,"toolAction":"Testing AxisItem","toolSummary":"Test AxisItem in PyQt6"}}]}
